मण्डलम् वास्तु ॥

॰ ONE MODULE IN TWO FILES, STATED (W-225, 2026-09-04). `vastu.t1` also opens
॰ with `मण्डलम् वास्तु ॥`. That is not a rename waiting to happen and not a
॰ collision: `nirvahana.rs:458` keys a routine as `module ॱ name`, so both
॰ files register under `वास्तु`, and their declared names are DISJOINT — 47
॰ here (the AST: records, kinds, the two arenas), 6 there (the object model:
॰ `स्थापन`, `वस्तुसंज्ञा`, `पुनःस्थापनम्`, `शोधनखण्डः`, `वस्तु` and its
॰ fields' kinds) — so a caller writing `वास्तुॱवाक्य` or `वास्तुॱवस्तु`
॰ reaches exactly one definition. The two halves are the port of two Rust
॰ files, `t1/ast.rs` and `vastu.rs`, that happen to share a Sanskrit name
॰ ("the structure"): the AST is the structure of a program, the object the
॰ structure of a file. A name added to either file must not be a name the
॰ other declares; `t1_modules.rs` pins the pair and the disjointness.
॰ `vastu.t1`'s header says the same from its side.

॰ ADR-0030 REMEDIATION, TASK `D-002h`. THE FILE TAKEN BY THIS CYCLE IS THIS ONE.
॰ All 47 of its type positions read `अ६४` and now read `न६४`. Not one moves the
॰ other way: `ast.t1` holds NO signed quantity at all, where `ir.t1` held four.
॰ Every site here is a DISCRIMINANT numbered from १ or an INDEX into one of the
॰ two arenas at the foot of the file, and neither can be negative.
॰
॰ THE RUST TWIN IS `crates/sadhana/src/t1/ast.rs`, AND IT REACHES ONLY TWELVE OF
॰ THE THIRTY-FOUR KIND CONSTANTS BELOW. Its `Type` enum's five variants are the
॰ five `*प्रकारभेद` in the same order, and `SymbolId(pub usize)` is what a
॰ `सूचकाङ्क` is — every integer `ast.rs` declares is unsigned.
॰ `NodeId(pub usize)` STOOD BESIDE IT HERE UNTIL 2026-09-05 and was DELETED by
॰ `W-274`: it was `pub`, constructed nowhere, and its only use was the map
॰ `Resolver::resolved_symbols`, deleted in the same row. The unsigned claim is
॰ unchanged — it lost a witness, not a counterexample.
॰ But its `Expression` has FIVE variants where this file declares eight, its
॰ `Statement` has TWO where this file declares eight, and it has no operator
॰ type at all; `ast.rs:36` and `:45` defer all three in as many words. So for
॰ TWENTY-TWO of these sites the twin has nothing to read, and the sign is read
॰ off what the constant is instead. Each line below says which case it is.
॰
॰ `crates/sadhana/src/t1/passes.rs` IS NOT A TWIN AND MAY NOT BE READ AS ONE:
॰ it is absent from `t1/mod.rs`, so it is never compiled, and its test writes
॰ `Expression::BinaryOp`, `BinaryOp::Add` and a `Declaration::Function` with an
॰ `is_public` field — three things `ast.rs` does not have. A file that does not
॰ build cannot say what a quantity's sign is.

॰ ॥ १०१ AND NOT १ ॥ W-171, 2026-10-01. `प्रकारपठनम्` stores every type node
॰ in `अभिव्यञ्जककोश`, so this family shares one `भेद` field with the
॰ expression kinds below; at १..५ the two families collided and a kind-१
॰ node was ambiguous. The base १०० keeps them disjoint with headroom — the
॰ expression family is at १३ and growing. Disjoint ranges close the hazard;
॰ the owner's 2026-09-01 decision (a separate arena behind `प्रकार`) is a
॰ distinct, undelivered step and this renumbering does not pre-empt it.
सार्वजनिक चरः मूलप्रकारभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १०१ ।  ॰ Type::Primitive(String)
सार्वजनिक चरः खण्डप्रकारभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १०२ । ॰ Type::Slice(Box<Type>)
सार्वजनिक चरः स्थानम्प्रकारभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १०३ । ॰ Type::Pointer(Box<Type>)
सार्वजनिक चरः सम्भाव्यप्रकारभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १०४ । ॰ Type::Optional(Box<Type>)
सार्वजनिक चरः दोषयुक्तप्रकारभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १०५ । ॰ Type::ErrorUnion(Box<Type>)

