॰ ॥ शेषः AND बृहत्समम् ॥ ADR-0037, by owner decision 2026-09-02.
॰
॰ ADR-0032 recorded both as absent "so nobody re-derives it", and each entry
॰ failed differently. MODULO: its evidence -- the corpus`s `शेषः` tokens are
॰ all a LOCAL VARIABLE -- was TRUE on 2026-08-30, and `encode.t1:647`s
॰ operator use is dated 08-31, the day AFTER. The ADR was overtaken.
॰ `>=`: it asked whether `न्यूनसमम्` and `अधिकसमम्` appear. The corpus writes
॰ `बृहत्समम्`, and `vakyavibhaga.t1:3163` has carried it since 08-29, the day
॰ BEFORE. That search used the LEXICON`s vocabulary inside an ADR whose
॰ principle is that the CORPUS is canonical -- a census keyed to a candidate
॰ list can only find candidates.
॰
॰ Neither is a new precedence level: `शेषः` sits with `गुणनम्`/`विभाजनम्` and
॰ `बृहत्समम्` with the comparisons, so ADR-0032`s ladder is unchanged.
सार्वजनिक चरः शेषद्विकर्मभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १४ ।
सार्वजनिक चरः बृहत्समद्विकर्मभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १५ ।

