॰ ॥ बूलाभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॥ `सत्यम्` and `असत्यम्` — added 2026-09-01.
॰
॰ `spec/grammar-t1.ebnf:138` lists them among the KEYWORDS, "true / false",
॰ so they are no more identifiers than `यदि` is. `व्याकर` built a
॰ `नामाभिव्यञ्जक` for each and `अर्थ` then refused them as undeclared — the
॰ correct answer to the wrong question. The corpus writes the two words 552
॰ times across 15 sources, so this alone refused most files.
॰
॰ WHY A NINTH KIND AND NOT A NUMERAL. Spelling a boolean as `अङ्काभिव्यञ्जक`
॰ would need no new constant and would LIE ABOUT THE TYPE; `प्रकारपरीक्षा`
॰ would then have to unpick it, which is a worse debt than a constant. The
॰ divergence from `ast.rs` is deliberate and already the rule here: its
॰ `Expression` has five variants against this corpus`s eight and `:36`
॰ defers the rest out loud.
॰ `मूल्यसूचकाङ्क` carries the token, so सत्यम् and असत्यम् are told apart by
॰ TEXT, exactly as a numeral`s value is.
सार्वजनिक चरः बूलाभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ९ ।

॰ ॥ शून्याभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॥ `शून्यम्` — added 2026-09-01, same reason as ९.
॰ `spec/grammar-t1.ebnf:137` lists it among the KEYWORDS, "void", and the
॰ corpus writes it 268 times — almost always as the value a `सम्भाव्य` is
॰ compared against. `व्याकर` built a `नामाभिव्यञ्जक` for each and `अर्थ`
॰ refused it as undeclared: the correct answer to the wrong question, and
॰ the single largest cause of refusal left in the corpus.
सार्वजनिक चरः शून्याभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १० ।

॰ ॥ समावेशाभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॥ `embed = "समावेशः" , "आरभ्य" , identifier ,
॰ "समाप्तम्"` — `spec/grammar-t1.ebnf:341`, ADR-0019. `मूल्यसूचकाङ्क` holds
॰ the TABLE`s name token, which is the only name in it to resolve.
॰ `समावेशः` is a KEYWORD (:135), so without this arm it became a नाम and the
॰ embed`s table became its ARGUMENT — two undeclared names where the source
॰ has one construct. It is how `samyojana.t1` and `sanskrit_text.t1` read a
॰ generated table, and it accounted for two of the seven refusals left.
सार्वजनिक चरः समावेशाभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ११ ।

॰ ॥ ऋणाभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॥ `unary_expr = { unary_op } , call_expr` with
॰ `unary_op = "ऋण"` — :659 and :628. `वामसूचकाङ्क` holds the operand.
॰ SPACED, and that spacing is the whole distinction: `lex.t1` notes that the
॰ sign is INSIDE the token with no space allowed, so `ऋण१` is ONE token and a
॰ negative numeral, while `ऋण सीमा` is TWO and is this production.
सार्वजनिक चरः ऋणाभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १२ ।

॰ ॥ खण्डाभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॥ `slice = index , postfix_expr` — W-228, 2026-09-04.
॰ THE INTERPRETER'S READING, NOW THE GRAMMAR'S: an `अङ्कः … अन्तः` followed by
॰ anything that can begin an argument is a SLICE and never a further argument
॰ (`nirvahana.rs`'s `postfix`, measured over every index in the corpus).
॰ `वामसूचकाङ्क` holds the `सूचकाङ्काभिव्यञ्जक` — the base and the lower bound,
॰ reused rather than respelled — and `दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क` the limit. 20 corpus
॰ sites read as a call on an index before this kind existed. The resolver
॰ reaches both children through its default arm; `अभिव्यञ्जकप्रकारः` types it
॰ as it types an index, which is not yet; `मध्यरूप` gives it the stub every
॰ unported kind gets (ir.t1 is W-204's lane). ONE `न६४` binding: the ledger
॰ in `grammar_t1.rs` says so in the same commit.
सार्वजनिक चरः खण्डाभिव्यञ्जकभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १३ ।

सार्वजनिक संरचना अभिव्यञ्जक आरभ्य
    भेद ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                            ॰ which of the thirteen kinds above
    मूल्यसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                  ॰ Identifier/Numeral/StringLiteral's String, as an index
    वामसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                    ॰ first operand: index into अभिव्यञ्जककोश
    ॰ FOR उक्ताभिव्यञ्जक, A TOKEN INDEX — `W-215`: the closing `इति`, so the
    ॰ content is the tokens मूल्यसूचकाङ्क..दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क exclusive.
    दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                 ॰ second operand: index into अभिव्यञ्जककोश — and on a नामाभिव्यञ्जक, W-228 (b): the MEMBER TOKEN's index (exact, taken before अग्रिमम्) of a spaced qualifier `मण्डल ॱ नाम` folded into the name; ० otherwise
    द्विकर्म ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                       ॰ which of the fifteen operator kinds
    ॰ W-183 (2026-09-03): the SymbolId the resolver found for an Identifier, PLUS ONE —
    ॰ symbols number from ० (`निर्णायकारम्भः`), so ० here means UNRESOLVED and n means
    ॰ symbol n-1. Written by `अर्थ ॱ अभिव्यञ्जकनिर्णयः`, read by `अभिव्यञ्जकप्रकारः`;
    ॰ a checker run on an unresolved program sees ० everywhere and keeps its old answer.
    संज्ञासूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४
समाप्तम् ।

सार्वजनिक चरः अभिव्यञ्जकवाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ । ॰ Statement::Expression(Expression)
सार्वजनिक चरः समूहवाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।  ॰ Statement::Block(Vec<Statement>)
सार्वजनिक चरः चरवाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।    ॰ no `ast.rs` variant — `:45` defers it
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रत्यागमनवाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ । ॰ no `ast.rs` variant — `:45` defers it
सार्वजनिक चरः आयातवाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।  ॰ no `ast.rs` variant — `:45` defers it
सार्वजनिक चरः यदिवाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ६ ।   ॰ no `ast.rs` variant — `:45` defers it
सार्वजनिक चरः यावत्वाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ७ । ॰ no `ast.rs` variant — `:45` defers it
सार्वजनिक चरः समवाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ८ ।    ॰ no `ast.rs` variant — `:45` defers it

सार्वजनिक संरचना वाक्य आरभ्य
    भेद ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                            ॰ which of the eight kinds above
    ॰ THE STATEMENT'S FIRST TOKEN — `W-240`. This field was `स्थान ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः
    ॰ अ८`, a run of octets that `वाक्ययोजनम्` never wrote and no pass ever read:
    ॰ every statement carried a location nobody could name it by, and a
    ॰ refusal one level above a name (`अनिर्णीतपङ्क्ति` closed that gap for
    ॰ names, W-191) had no line to give. A token index, as `मूल्यसूचकाङ्क`
    ॰ is; ० for a statement no source wrote (one pushed by a test by hand).
    स्थानसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ
    वामसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                    ॰ index into अभिव्यञ्जककोश or वाक्यकोश
    दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                  ॰ index into अभिव्यञ्जककोश or वाक्यकोश
    ॰ THE `अन्यथा` BODY OF A `यदि`, ० when there is none — `W-198`. Until then
    ॰ `व्याकरॱवाक्यपठनम्` parsed the else body into `अन्यशरीर` and had NO SLOT
    ॰ to keep it in, so every `अन्यथा` body in the corpus was parsed and
    ॰ dropped, and no stage after the parser could see one. Written as ० by
    ॰ `वाक्ययोजनम्` and filled by the `यदि` arm AFTER the push — copy, modify,
    ॰ write back — so the appender keeps its arity and no caller changes, the
    ॰ same reasoning `आदिसूचकाङ्क` gives below. A statement index, like
    ॰ `दक्षिणसूचकाङ्क` is for `यदि`; ० is "no child", never slot ०.
    अन्यसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ
    ॰ THE FIRST INDEX OF THIS STATEMENT'S OWN SUBTREE — added 2026-09-01, and
    ॰ it is what lets a walker see a block's DIRECT children.
    ॰
    ॰ `व्याकरॱवाक्ययोजनम्` takes its children as ALREADY-PUSHED indices and
    ॰ numbers itself after, so a child always has a LOWER index than its parent
    ॰ and every subtree is a CONTIGUOUS range ending at the node itself. A
    ॰ block is the range प्रथम..अन्तिम, so a nested block's statements lie
    ॰ inside its parent's range too. Iterating that range resolves them TWICE —
    ॰ the second time in the enclosing scope, where they do not belong — and
    ॰ घोषणम् refuses a duplicate, so a VALID program is reported as having one.
    ॰ `अर्थ ॱ वाक्यनिर्णयः` is stubbed on exactly that, and मध्य waits on it too.
    ॰
    ॰ WHY THE SUBTREE START AND NOT THE NEXT SIBLING, which is what those notes
    ॰ ask for: a next sibling CANNOT BE COMPUTED AT PUSH TIME — when a node is
    ॰ pushed its next sibling does not exist yet. This can: it is the minimum of
    ॰ its children's, or the node's own index when it has none, and every input
    ॰ is in hand at the moment of the push. It also needs NO new argument, so
    ॰ `वाक्ययोजनम्` keeps its arity and no caller changes.
    ॰
    ॰ Walk a block's direct children from the TOP, skipping whole subtrees:
    ॰     क्रमः भवति अन्तिम ।
    ॰     यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् प्रथम समम् असत्यम् आदि
    ॰         ॰ visit क्रमः
    ॰         क्रमः भवति आरभ्य आदिसूचकाङ्क वियोगः १ समाप्तम् ।
    ॰     इति
    ॰ (`अधिकसमम्` is a lexicon proposal with NO grammar production, so the
    ॰ bound is spelled `न्यूनम्` inverted.)
    आदिसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ
    ॰ W-183 (2026-09-03): a `चर` statement's DECLARED TYPE — an अभिव्यञ्जककोश index
    ॰ (what `प्रकारपठनम्` answers), ० when none. The parser read it and DROPPED it
    ॰ until this field existed; `वाक्ययोजनम्` writes ० and the `चर` arm fills it in.
    प्रकारसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४
समाप्तम् ।

